    "title": "Garfield County 15-year-old last seen at Denver's Union Station bus area: sheriff - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Heather Willard ,\n1 hours ago\nDENVER (KDVR) — A 15-year-old girl is missing from the Carbondale area of Garfield County , according to the county sheriff’s office.\nGrace Campise, 15, was last seen at about 5:15 a.m. on Wednesday at the bus area of Union Station in Denver. She was reported missing from the Carbondale area, according to the Garfield County Sheriff’s Office.\nMissing man with seizure disorder last seen Sept. 1: Arapahoe County Sheriff’s Office The agency said the teen was last seen wearing a black romper with cut sleeves and pink pajama pants worn over it.\nCampise is described as being 5 feet, 2 inches tall with long brown hair with blonde highlights, blue eyes, and weighing about 100 pounds. The sheriff’s office said that Campis also has a “large, swollen scar on one shoulder” and a nose piercing.\nGrace Campise, 15, of Carbondale, was last seen at about 5:15 a.m. on Wednesday at the bus area of Union Station in Denver. (Courtesy the Garfield County Sheriff’s Office) Anyone with information about the teen’s whereabouts is asked to call Garfield County Emergency Communications Authority at 970-625-8095 for a non-emergency line, or 911.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX31 Denver.",
